            <ArticleTitle>[Seasonal cold adaptation as a risk factor in ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>19-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Seasonal variations (with a peak in winter and a fall in summer) in the level of arachidonic acid in low-density lipids, in heart rate, and blood pressures were studied in patients with angina pectoris. The findings are required for a better understanding the mechanism and for development of preventive measures against ischemic heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
